-- title:
--   Closed neighbourhoods of a finite set of points
-- statement:
--   For a finite set $A$ of points in a metric space $M$ and $\delta\ge0$, the closed $\delta$-neighbourhood is
--   $$
--   \mathrm{Near}(A,\delta)=\{x\in M:\ d(x,a)\le\delta\ \text{for some }a\in A\}.
--   $$
--
--   It is the union of the closed balls of radius $\delta$ about the points of $A$. It is used to reduce supports of free-space elements to neighbourhoods of finite nets.
